# Normalise line endings.
#
# Without this, Git on Windows commits CRLF while the Docker container, CI,
# and any Linux collaborator use LF -- so a file someone merely opened shows
# every line as changed. `text=auto eol=lf` stores LF in the repository
# regardless of the OS that wrote the file.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Files that must keep LF even locally: shell scripts break with CRLF, and
# anything Docker executes runs on Linux.
*.sh   text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf

# Binary -- never diffed, never line-ending converted.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.xlsx binary
